# Forth Interpreter with Stack Visualization

A complete Forth language interpreter written in x86-64 assembly language with real-time stack visualization.

## Features

### Core Features
- Complete stack-based virtual machine
- Arithmetic operations (+, -, *, /, %)
- Stack manipulation (dup, drop, swap, over, rot)
- Output operations (., emit, cr, space)
- Input parsing and tokenization
- Professional terminal-based GUI with colors

### Bonus Features
- Real-time stack visualization
- Error handling with colored messages
- Stack bounds checking
- Command history (via terminal)
- Help system
- Clean, professional interface

## Commands

### Arithmetic
- `+` - Addition (a b -- a+b)
- `-` - Subtraction (a b -- a-b)
- `*` - Multiplication (a b -- a*b)
- `/` - Division (a b -- a/b)
- `%` - Modulus (a b -- a%b)

### Stack Manipulation
- `dup` - Duplicate top of stack
- `drop` - Remove top of stack
- `swap` - Swap top two items
- `over` - Copy second item to top
- `rot` - Rotate third item to top
- `clear` - Clear entire stack
- `.s` - Print entire stack

### Output
- `.` - Print top number
- `emit` - Print character (ASCII)
- `cr` - New line
- `space` - Print space

### Control Flow (Basic)
- `if` - Conditional execution
- `else` - Alternative branch
- `then` - End conditional
- `begin` - Start loop
- `until` - Loop until condition

### System
- `help` - Show help
- `bye` - Exit interpreter

## Building and Running

### Prerequisites
- NASM (Netwide Assembler)
- LD (GNU Linker)
- Linux Mint (or any Linux distribution)

